Aim: To read an image in Python using OpenCV and convert the original color image into a grayscale image.
Observation:
- The original image contains three color channels: Blue, Green, and Red (BGR).
- The grayscale image contains only intensity values ranging from 0 to 255.
- The image appears in shades of black, white, and gray.
Result: The input color image was successfully read and converted into a grayscale image using OpenCV.
